# The Vistani camp outside Vallaki's west gate (docs/voice/arrigal.md, luvash.md, arabelle.md, bluto.md, vistana.md).
# arrigal greets newcomers; luvash grieves for Arabelle; the vistana at the fire saw the fisherman; bluto is on the
# lakeshore with a sack; arabelle, once home.

~ arrigal
if not flag.vistani_camp_met
set vistani_camp_met
Narrator: A lean man in a black coat and a silver-buttoned waistcoat rises from the steps of a painted wagon, unhurried, as though he'd been expecting you since before you set out.
Arrigal: Welcome, travellers. You're far from the road for honest folk and close to the lake for clever ones. Sit at our fire. It costs nothing, tonight.
if tarokka.drawn or flag.madam_eva_rumor
Arrigal: You've sat at Madam Eva's table, I think. It's on you like woodsmoke.
endif
if flag.tser_pool_brawl_won
Arrigal [angry]: And you've spilled our blood at Tser Pool. Every camp in the valley knows your faces now. You may sit at this fire because I say so, and for no other reason.
elif flag.vistani_robbed and not flag.vistani_repaid
Arrigal: Stanimir's strongbox came up forty gold light after your visit. Our people count, friend. We always count.
elif flag.nicu_kin_told
Arrigal: You brought word of Nicu to his people, at the crossroads. That was decently done. We remember decency too.
endif
if guest:ireena
Narrator: His eyes go to Ireena and stay there, politely, the way a merchant's eyes stay on a price.
Arrigal: And the burgomaster's daughter. Our wagons go where his carriages can't, lady. If you ever want to be somewhere he isn't, you need only ask me.
Ireena: I've been offered rides by strangers before. I walked.
endif
else
if flag.arrigal_chest_opened
Arrigal: Someone has been in my strongbox. I won't ask who. I'll simply remember.
endif
if flag.vallaki_backed == "wachter"
Arrigal [smile]: Lady Wachter's town now, I hear. Our lord will be pleased. Our wagons are always welcome where he's pleased.
else
Arrigal: Back at our fire. You're becoming regulars.
endif
endif
-> arrigal_menu

~ arrigal_menu
* Why isn't anyone out looking for the headman's daughter? -> arabelle_q
* What news on the roads? -> roads
* [if guest:ireena] [Insight DC 15] What does he want with Ireena? -> insight_ok | insight_fail
* [if flag.arrigal_suspected] You'd sell her to the castle. -> accuse
* [name:tamsin_tealeaf] [if flag.locket_coach_known and not flag.locket_arrigal_confirmed] Ask about the black carriage that drives itself. -> companions/locket:arrigal
* Goodbye. -> END

~ arabelle_q
Arrigal: Luvash's girl wandered off. Children do. My brother drinks, which is how he looks for things. The lake will give her back, or it won't. That's the way of lakes.
if name:thistle
interject name:thistle: That's a cold answer for an uncle. He's lying. Smells like it.
else
interject tag:blunt: That's a cold answer for an uncle.
endif
Arrigal: It's a cold valley.
-> arrigal_menu

~ roads
Arrigal: The roads are his, like everything else. They're quiet for those he wants to arrive, and less quiet for the others. You arrived. Draw your own conclusions.
-> arrigal_menu

~ insight_ok
set arrigal_suspected
Narrator: The offer is sincere in one way only: he'd carry her somewhere, gladly, and very quickly. You've seen that look on men selling horses they've already sold to someone else.
-> arrigal_menu

~ insight_fail
Narrator: He's charming, and calm, and impossible to read. That may be the whole of him. It may not.
-> arrigal_menu

~ accuse
Arrigal [smile]: I sell nothing, my friend. I carry messages. Some of them are about you. You'll find our people do the same everywhere in this valley, and live longer for it.
-> arrigal_menu

~ luvash
if flag.arabelle_rescued
-> luvash_grateful
endif
if flag.arabelle_lost
Narrator: Luvash sits on the step of his wagon with an empty bottle and doesn't look up when you come.
Luvash [sad]: You tried. They tell me you tried. Go away now. Please.
-> END
endif
if not flag.luvash_met
set luvash_met
quest missing_arabelle asked
Narrator: A huge man in a red sash sits on the steps of his wagon with a bottle in each hand, shouting at the camp, at the lake, at the sky. The camp walks around him without looking.
endif
Luvash [angry]: Go away! Unless you've come to find my girl. Have you come to find my girl? Arabelle. Seven years old. Black hair. Gone from her bed since last night, and my brother says she wandered!
* We'll find her. -> promise
* Tell us what happened. -> what
* Goodbye. -> END

~ promise
attitude luvash friendly
Luvash: You will? Strangers? None of my own people will, because Arrigal says not to. Find her and I'll owe you more than I have. Ask at the fire. Somebody saw something. Somebody always sees something.
approve kip_smudgewick +2 godrick_pendlebrook +2 thistle +1: You promised Luvash you'd find his daughter
-> END

~ what
Luvash [sad]: She was in her bed when I went to sleep. In the morning, the bed was cold and the wagon door was open. She never opens the door. She's afraid of the lake.
-> luvash

~ luvash_grateful
set vistani_friends
Narrator: Luvash has Arabelle on his knee and both arms round her, and he is not drinking.
Luvash [smile]: My friends. My friends! Every Vistani wagon in Barovia is your wagon now. Every fire is your fire. I've told them. I've told them all.
if tarokka.ally.npc == arabelle and not guest:arabelle
Arabelle: I'm going with them, Papa. The cards said. I saw it before they did.
Luvash [afraid]: No. No! I only just got you back!
Arabelle: You'll get me back again. I've seen that too.
* Arabelle, stay with your father. -> arabelle_stays
* We'll keep her safe, Luvash. On our lives. -> arabelle_joins
endif
if not flag.arabelle_reward_given
set arabelle_reward_given
gold +50
Luvash: Take this. It's not enough. Nothing would be enough.
Luvash: And this. My grandmother swam the Luna in it, all the way to the falls and back. In the water it makes you a fish. The lake took my girl once; let it never take you.
give cloak_of_the_manta_ray
endif
-> END

~ arabelle_stays
Arabelle: All right. But you'll want me later, at the end. You'll see.
approve kip_smudgewick +1: You left Arabelle with her father
-> END

~ arabelle_joins
Luvash [sad]: On your lives. I'll hold you to every one of them.
join arabelle
quest find_the_ally found
Arabelle: Don't worry, Papa. I know how this part goes.
-> END

~ vistana
if flag.arabelle_rescued
Vistana [smile]: The girl's home. Luvash is sober. Two miracles in one week. We'll have to move camp; the luck won't last.
-> END
endif
Vistana: Sit, if you like. Don't touch the horses. Don't ask about the fortunes; I'm off duty.
if quest.missing_arabelle == asked
-> vistana_clue
endif
-> END

~ vistana_clue
* We're looking for Arabelle. Did you see anything? -> clue
* Goodbye. -> END

~ clue
quest missing_arabelle clue
Vistana: I saw a man on the shore last night, after the moon went down. Bluto, the fisherman from town, the one with no fish. He had a sack over his shoulder, and the sack was moving.
Vistana: I told Arrigal. Arrigal said fishermen carry sacks. Go north to the water. Hurry.
-> END

~ bluto
Narrator: Up to his thighs in the black water, a gaunt man in a sodden coat is wading out from the shore with a sack over his shoulder. The sack is kicking.
Bluto: Stay back! Stay back! The lake's hungry. A whole year without a fish. She wants something better than worms, she does, and then the nets'll fill!
* [Persuasion DC 13] Talk him back to the shore. -> talk_ok | talk_fail
* [Intimidation DC 13] Tell him exactly what happens to him if he lets go of that sack. -> scare_ok | scare_fail
* [Athletics DC 12] Charge into the water and grab the sack. -> grab_ok | grab_fail

~ talk_ok
Narrator: He listens. He doesn't want to, but he listens, and halfway through he starts crying, and the sack slides off his shoulder into your arms.
-> rescued

~ scare_ok
Narrator: He looks at your faces and does the sum. He drops the sack in the shallows and runs, splashing, into the reeds.
-> rescued

~ grab_ok
Narrator: You hit the water running. Bluto swings at you with a fist like a wet stone and misses, and you have the sack before he can try again.
-> rescued

~ talk_fail
Bluto: No! She told me! She told me in the dark!
Narrator: He heaves the sack out into the deep water. It hits with a slap and sinks at once.
-> dive

~ scare_fail
Bluto: You can't scare me worse than she does!
Narrator: He heaves the sack out into the deep water. It hits with a slap and sinks at once.
-> dive

~ grab_fail
Narrator: The lakebed goes out from under your feet. By the time you're up again, spluttering, Bluto has thrown the sack into the deep water.
-> dive

~ dive
cutscene arabelle_dive
Narrator: Someone has to go in after it. The water is black and cold enough to stop a heart.
check Athletics DC 13 -> rescued | dive_again

~ dive_again
Narrator: Nothing. Weed, and cold, and dark. Up for air. Down again, deeper.
check Perception DC 12 -> rescued | lost

~ rescued
set arabelle_rescued
quest missing_arabelle rescued
Narrator: Inside the sack is a small girl, soaked, furious and very much alive, with black hair plastered over a solemn face. Bluto has gone, somewhere in the reeds.
Arabelle: You took a long time. The water was cold. The fish-man is sad; don't hurt him. He'll go in the lake himself, in the end. I've seen it.
if name:kip_smudgewick
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Hello, miss. We're very glad you're not drowned. Apricot? No charge. You must be starving.
else
interject tag:cheerful: Hello. We're very glad you're not drowned.
endif
Arabelle: So am I. Take me to my father. He'll be drinking. He drinks when he's frightened.
approve kip_smudgewick +3 godrick_pendlebrook +2 liriel_dawnsong +2 thistle +2 wren_featherfoot +1 ratatoille +1: You pulled Arabelle out of the lake
-> END

~ lost
set arabelle_lost
quest missing_arabelle lost
Narrator: When you come up the last time, the water is flat and black and empty, and Bluto has gone, somewhere in the reeds. There is nothing in your hands but lake weed.
interject class:cleric: Morninglord keep her. We'll tell her father. Somebody has to.
-> END

~ arabelle
Arabelle: Hello again.
if flag.vallaki_backed == "wachter"
Arabelle: The lady with the teapot sits in the big chair now. She thinks she's safe. She isn't. Nobody near him is.
elif flag.vallaki_backed == "baron"
Arabelle: The fat man will hold a festival every week until he runs out of suns.
elif flag.vallaki_backed == "neither"
Arabelle: The priest and the bird-man run the town now. The birds are pleased. You can tell by the way they sit.
elif guest:ireena
Arabelle: Your red-haired friend has been to the lake before. A long time ago. She'll go again, one day. I don't like that part.
else
Arabelle: One of you is going to lie to the man in the castle, and he's going to like it. I don't know which one. I'd tell you if I did.
endif
-> END
